/-!
# The locally free locus of a complex-and-divisor situation

Let `(X, D, M)` be a triple as in Situation 0F8S.  Stacks tag 0F8W speaks of the maximal open
subscheme `W ⊂ X` over which the cohomology sheaves of `M` are locally free, and asserts that
the morphism `b : X' ⟶ X` of tag 0GTY is an isomorphism over `W`.

This file introduces that open subscheme, as the finite free cohomology locus of the perfect
object `M` of tag 0GT1, and proves tag 0F8W along the lines of its own proof.  Over an affine
chart `(U, A, f, M^•)` contained in `W` the determinantal ideals `I_i(M^•, f)` are, near every
prime of `A`, generated by a power of `f` — this is More on Algebra, tag 0GSV — and hence so is
the centre `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` in which tag 0GTY blows the chart up.  Since `f` is a
nonzerodivisor, that centre is an effective Cartier divisor, so blowing up in it changes
nothing (tag 0807); as the charts contained in `W` cover `W`, the morphism `b` is an
isomorphism over `W`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.locallyFreeLocus`: the open subscheme `W ⊂ X`,
  namely the set of points at which every cohomology stalk of `M` is a finite free module over
  the local ring of `X`.  It is open because `M` is perfect, by tag 0GT1.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.AffineChart.blowupCentreIdealSheaf`: the centre
  `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` of the blowup of tag 0GTY over an affine chart, read as an ideal sheaf on
  the affine open subscheme `U` rather than as an ideal of `Γ(X, U)`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.le_locallyFreeLocus`: `W` is the largest open
  subscheme over which the cohomology sheaves of `M` are finite locally free; this is the
  maximality half of tag 0GT1 read in the situation.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.isPullbackDefined_locallyFreeLocus`: the
  pullback of `D` to `W` is defined, so that the triple restricted to `W` is again a triple as
  in Situation 0F8S.
* `AffineChart.exists_away_map_blowupCentre_eq_span_pow_of_le_locallyFreeLocus`: on an affine
  chart contained in `W` the centre of the blowup of tag 0GTY is, near every prime, generated
  by a power of the equation `f` of the divisor.  This is the first sentence of the proof of
  tag 0F8W.
* `AffineChart.isIso_blowUpToBase_of_le_locallyFreeLocus`: hence the blowing up of such a
  chart in that centre is an isomorphism, which is the second sentence of that proof.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.isIso_pullback_snd_locallyFreeLocus`: **tag
  0F8W**, a morphism which over every affine chart is the blowing up of the chart in the
  product of its determinantal ideals is an isomorphism over `W`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.IsGoodBlowup.isIso_resLE_of_isGoodOver`: a
  morphism `b` with properties (1) and (2) of tag 0GTY restricts to an isomorphism over an open
  subscheme `V ⊂ X` whose inclusion is good for the triple, provided the restriction of `b` to
  `b⁻¹V` is also good for the triple.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.IsGoodBlowup.isIso_resLE_locallyFreeLocus`: the
  same statement for `V = W`.

## The shape of tag 0F8W here

`AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.isIso_pullback_snd_locallyFreeLocus` states tag
0F8W for an arbitrary morphism `b` described the way tag 0GTY describes it — over each affine
chart, `b` is the blowing up of that chart in the product of its determinantal ideals — and for
an arbitrary open subscheme `W` whose affine charts inside it cover it.  Both descriptions hold
for the morphism tag 0GTY produces,
`AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.goodBlowupToBase`: the first by
`AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.AffineChart.existsUnique_iso_preimage_blowUp`, the
second because the chart domains form a basis of the topology of `X`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.exists_chart_mem_le`).  Tag 0F8W for that
morphism itself, with both discharged, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.isIso_pullback_snd_goodBlowupToBase_locallyFreeLocus`
in `GoodBlowupLocallyFree.lean`.

`AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.IsGoodBlowup.isIso_resLE_of_isGoodOver` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.IsGoodBlowup.isIso_resLE_locallyFreeLocus` take
the other route to the same conclusion, through the universal property of `b` rather than
through its affine-chart description; what they ask for instead is the goodness of the open
immersion `W ⟶ X` and of `b⁻¹W ⟶ X`, which is the affine-chart pullback of tag 0F8T.

## Implementation notes

The centre of the blowup lives as an ideal of `Γ(X, U)`, while an ideal sheaf on the affine
open subscheme `U` is built from an ideal of `Γ(U, ⊤)`; the two rings are identified by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.topIso`, and the local description of the centre is carried
across that isomorphism by matching the two standard open neighbourhoods with
`IsLocalization.ringEquivOfRingEquiv`.

Globalisation from the charts to `W` is `IsZariskiLocalAtTarget.of_openCover` for the property
of being an isomorphism, applied to the cover of `W` by the affine charts contained in it.

"Isomorphism over `V`" is expressed as `IsIso (b.resLE V (b ⁻¹ᵁ V) le_rfl)`, the restriction of
`b` to the open subscheme `b⁻¹V` of `X'` and `V` of `X`; `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.resLE` is
Mathlib's restriction of a morphism to opens of source and target, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι` is the square it sits in.  The lift of the inclusion
of `V` through `b` is pushed into `b⁻¹V` by the universal property of the open immersion
`(b ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι`, and the two composites are identified by the uniqueness clauses: one of them by
the monomorphy of `V.ι`, the other by the uniqueness of factorizations of `(b ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι ≫ b`
through `b`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F8W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F8W)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F8S](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F8S)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GTY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GTY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GT1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GT1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GSV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GSV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0807](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0807)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory StrictlyPerfect

universe u d

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation

variable (S : ComplexAndDivisorSituation.{u, d})

/-- **The locally free locus of a triple `(X, D, M)` as in Situation 0F8S.**  This is the
maximal open subscheme `W ⊂ X` over which the cohomology sheaves of `M` are locally free, as it
appears in Stacks tag 0F8W: the set of points at which every cohomology stalk of `M` is a finite
free module over the local ring of `X`, which is open because `M` is perfect by tag 0GT1. -/
def locallyFreeLocus : S.X.Opens :=
  ⟨RingedSpace.cohomologyFiniteFreeLocus S.M,
    RingedSpace.isOpen_cohomologyFiniteFreeLocus S.M S.isPerfect⟩

/-- A point of `X` lies in the locally free locus exactly when all the cohomology stalks of `M`
there are finite free modules over the local ring of `X` at that point. -/
theorem mem_locallyFreeLocus_iff (x : S.X) :
    x ∈ S.locallyFreeLocus ↔ ∀ i : ℤ,
      Module.Free (ToType (S.X.presheaf.stalk x))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk
            ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (OXMod.{u, u} S.X.toRingedSpace) i).obj
              S.M).val.presheaf x)) ∧
        Module.Finite (ToType (S.X.presheaf.stalk x))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk
            ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (OXMod.{u, u} S.X.toRingedSpace) i).obj
              S.M).val.presheaf x)) :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- **The maximality of the locally free locus**, which is the maximality half of Stacks tag
0GT1 read in Situation 0F8S: every open subscheme of `X` over which all the cohomology sheaves
of `M` are finite locally free is contained in `W`. -/
theorem le_locallyFreeLocus (V : S.X.Opens)
    (hV : ∀ i : ℤ, RingedSpace.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOver
      ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (OXMod.{u, u} S.X.toRingedSpace) i).obj S.M) V) :
    V ≤ S.locallyFreeLocus :=
  RingedSpace.subset_cohomologyFiniteFreeLocus S.M V hV

/-- The pullback of the effective Cartier divisor `D` along the inclusion of an open subscheme
is defined, the inclusion being flat.  In particular this holds for the locally free locus, so
that the triple restricted to `W` is again a triple as in Situation 0F8S. -/
theorem isPullbackDefined_ι (V : S.X.Opens) :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsPullbackDefined V.ι S.D :=
  Stacks.Divisors.isPullbackDefined_of_flat V.ι S.D S.isEffectiveCartierDivisor

/-- The pullback of `D` to the locally free locus `W` is defined. -/
theorem isPullbackDefined_locallyFreeLocus :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsPullbackDefined S.locallyFreeLocus.ι S.D :=
  S.isPullbackDefined_ι _

namespace AffineChart

variable {S}

/-- **Stacks tag 0GSV read on an affine chart.**  At a prime of the coordinate ring at which
every cohomology module of the chart's complex becomes free, the determinantal ideal
`I_i(M^•, f)` becomes generated by a power of the equation `f` of the divisor. -/
theorem localized_determinantalIdeal_eq_span_pow (C : AffineChart S)
    (p : Ideal Γ(S.X, C.U)) [p.IsPrime]
    (hfree : ∀ i : ℤ, Module.Free (Localization.AtPrime p)
      (LocalizedModule p.primeCompl
        ((HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat Γ(S.X, C.U))
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ) i).obj C.complex.toCochainComplex)))
    (i : ℤ) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, (C.determinantalIdeal i).map (algebraMap Γ(S.X, C.U) (Localization.AtPrime p))
      = Ideal.span {algebraMap Γ(S.X, C.U) (Localization.AtPrime p) C.f ^ n} :=
  Stacks.DeterminantalIdeal.FreeHomology.localized_idealI_eq_span_pow_of_free_homology
    p C.f C.regular.mem_nonZeroDivisors C.complex hfree i

/-- The centre `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` of the blowup of an affine chart becomes generated by a power of
the equation `f` of the divisor at every prime at which the cohomology of the chart's complex is
free: a product of ideals each generated by a power of `f` is generated by a power of `f`. -/
theorem localized_blowupCentre_eq_span_pow (C : AffineChart S)
    (p : Ideal Γ(S.X, C.U)) [p.IsPrime]
    (hfree : ∀ i : ℤ, Module.Free (Localization.AtPrime p)
      (LocalizedModule p.primeCompl
        ((HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat Γ(S.X, C.U))
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ) i).obj C.complex.toCochainComplex))) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, C.blowupCentre.map (algebraMap Γ(S.X, C.U) (Localization.AtPrime p))
      = Ideal.span {algebraMap Γ(S.X, C.U) (Localization.AtPrime p) C.f ^ n} := by
  classical
  set φ := algebraMap Γ(S.X, C.U) (Localization.AtPrime p) with hφ
  choose n hn using C.localized_determinantalIdeal_eq_span_pow p hfree
  refine ⟨∑ i ∈ C.complex.bounded.toFinset, n i, ?_⟩
  rw [blowupCentre]
  induction C.complex.bounded.toFinset using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty => simp [hφ, Ideal.map_top]
  | insert a s ha ih =>
    rw [Finset.prod_insert ha, Finset.sum_insert ha, Ideal.map_mul, hn, ih, pow_add,
      Ideal.span_singleton_mul_span_singleton]

/-- **The first sentence of the proof of Stacks tag 0F8W.**  Near every prime at which the
cohomology of the chart's complex is free, the centre `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` of the blowup of an
affine chart is already generated by a power of the equation `f` of the divisor: the equality
of finitely generated ideals in the local ring descends to a standard open neighbourhood. -/
theorem exists_away_map_blowupCentre_eq_span_pow (C : AffineChart S)
    (p : Ideal Γ(S.X, C.U)) [p.IsPrime]
    (hfree : ∀ i : ℤ, Module.Free (Localization.AtPrime p)
      (LocalizedModule p.primeCompl
        ((HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat Γ(S.X, C.U))
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ) i).obj C.complex.toCochainComplex))) :
    ∃ g ∈ p.primeCompl, ∃ n : ℕ,
      C.blowupCentre.map (algebraMap Γ(S.X, C.U) (Localization.Away g))
        = Ideal.span {algebraMap Γ(S.X, C.U) (Localization.Away g) C.f ^ n} := by
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := C.localized_blowupCentre_eq_span_pow p hfree
  obtain ⟨g, hg, heq⟩ := Stacks.Localization.exists_mem_map_eq_map_localizationAway
    p.primeCompl (Localization.AtPrime p) C.blowupCentre_fg
    (Submodule.fg_span (Set.finite_singleton (C.f ^ n)))
    (by rw [hn, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, map_pow])
  exact ⟨g, hg, n, by rw [heq, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, map_pow]⟩

/-- The centre `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` of the blowup of an affine chart in Stacks tag 0GTY, read as an
ideal sheaf on the affine open subscheme `U` itself rather than as an ideal of `Γ(X, U)`. -/
noncomputable def blowupCentreIdealSheaf (C : AffineChart S) : C.U.1.toScheme.IdealSheafData :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (C.blowupCentre.map C.U.1.topIso.inv.hom)

/-- Being, near every prime, generated by a power of a fixed element is carried along a ring
isomorphism: the isomorphism matches the two standard open neighbourhoods. -/
private theorem exists_away_map_map_eq_span_pow {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    (e : A ≃+* B) (J : Ideal A) (a : A)
    (h : ∀ p : PrimeSpectrum A, ∃ g ∈ p.asIdeal.primeCompl, ∃ n : ℕ,
      J.map (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g))
        = Ideal.span {algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) a ^ n})
    (q : PrimeSpectrum B) :
    ∃ g ∈ q.asIdeal.primeCompl, ∃ n : ℕ,
      (J.map (e : A →+* B)).map (algebraMap B (Localization.Away g))
        = Ideal.span {algebraMap B (Localization.Away g) (e a) ^ n} := by
  obtain ⟨g, hg, n, hn⟩ := h (PrimeSpectrum.comap (e : A →+* B) q)
  have hmap : (Submonoid.powers g).map (e : A →* B) = Submonoid.powers (e g) :=
    Submonoid.map_powers _ _
  let ψ : Localization.Away g ≃+* Localization.Away (e g) :=
    IsLocalization.ringEquivOfRingEquiv (Localization.Away g) (Localization.Away (e g)) e hmap
  have hψ : ∀ x : A, (ψ : Localization.Away g →+* Localization.Away (e g))
      (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) x) = algebraMap B (Localization.Away (e g)) (e x) :=
    fun x => IsLocalization.ringEquivOfRingEquiv_eq hmap x
  have hcomp : (algebraMap B (Localization.Away (e g))).comp (e : A →+* B)
      = (ψ : Localization.Away g →+* Localization.Away (e g)).comp
          (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g)) :=
    RingHom.ext fun x => (hψ x).symm
  refine ⟨e g, hg, n, ?_⟩
  rw [Ideal.map_map, hcomp, ← Ideal.map_map, hn, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, map_pow,
    hψ a]

/-- **An affine chart whose centre is locally generated by a power of the equation of the
divisor carries an effective Cartier divisor.**  The equation `f` is a nonzerodivisor, so a
local generator `f ^ n` of the centre is one too, and local principality by a nonzerodivisor is
exactly the affine-local criterion of Stacks tag 01WS. -/
theorem isEffectiveCartierDivisor_blowupCentreIdealSheaf (C : AffineChart S)
    (hloc : ∀ p : PrimeSpectrum Γ(S.X, C.U), ∃ g ∈ p.asIdeal.primeCompl, ∃ n : ℕ,
      C.blowupCentre.map (algebraMap Γ(S.X, C.U) (Localization.Away g))
        = Ideal.span {algebraMap Γ(S.X, C.U) (Localization.Away g) C.f ^ n}) :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf := by
  let _ : IsAffine C.U.1.toScheme := C.U.2
  let e : Γ(S.X, C.U) ≃+* Γ(C.U.1.toScheme, ⊤) :=
    C.U.1.topIso.symm.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv
  have he : (e : Γ(S.X, C.U) →+* Γ(C.U.1.toScheme, ⊤)) = C.U.1.topIso.inv.hom := rfl
  have hreg : IsRegular (e C.f) := by
    rw [isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors, ← MulEquivClass.map_nonZeroDivisors e]
    exact ⟨C.f, C.regular.mem_nonZeroDivisors, rfl⟩
  refine Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_ofIdealTop_of_forall_exists_away
    (C.blowupCentre.map C.U.1.topIso.inv.hom) (e C.f) hreg fun q => ?_
  rw [← he]
  exact exists_away_map_map_eq_span_pow e C.blowupCentre C.f hloc q

/-- **The last sentence of the proof of Stacks tag 0F8W.**  If the centre `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` of
the blowup of an affine chart is locally generated by a power of the equation `f` of the
divisor, then the blowing up of the chart in that centre is an isomorphism: the centre is an
effective Cartier divisor, and blowing up an effective Cartier divisor changes nothing by
Stacks tag 0807. -/
theorem isIso_blowUpToBase_blowupCentreIdealSheaf (C : AffineChart S)
    (hloc : ∀ p : PrimeSpectrum Γ(S.X, C.U), ∃ g ∈ p.asIdeal.primeCompl, ∃ n : ℕ,
      C.blowupCentre.map (algebraMap Γ(S.X, C.U) (Localization.Away g))
        = Ideal.span {algebraMap Γ(S.X, C.U) (Localization.Away g) C.f ^ n}) :
    IsIso (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf) :=
  Stacks.Blowup.isIso_blowUpToBase_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor _
    (C.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_blowupCentreIdealSheaf hloc)

/-- **Stacks tag 0GSV on an affine chart inside the locally free locus.**  On an affine chart
contained in `W` the cohomology of the chart's complex is free in every local ring, so the
centre `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` of the blowup of the chart is, near every prime, generated by a power
of the equation `f` of the divisor.  This is the first sentence of the proof of Stacks tag
0F8W. -/
theorem exists_away_map_blowupCentre_eq_span_pow_of_le_locallyFreeLocus (C : AffineChart S)
    (hCW : C.U.1 ≤ S.locallyFreeLocus) (p : PrimeSpectrum Γ(S.X, C.U)) :
    ∃ g ∈ p.asIdeal.primeCompl, ∃ n : ℕ,
      C.blowupCentre.map (algebraMap Γ(S.X, C.U) (Localization.Away g))
        = Ideal.span {algebraMap Γ(S.X, C.U) (Localization.Away g) C.f ^ n} := by
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := exists_primeIdealOf_eq C.U.2 p
  exact C.exists_away_map_blowupCentre_eq_span_pow _
    fun i => C.free_localizedModule_homology_of_subset_cohomologyFiniteFreeLocus hCW x i

/-- **The affine-chart case of Stacks tag 0F8W.**  Over an affine chart contained in the
locally free locus `W` the centre `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` in which tag 0GTY blows the chart up is an
effective Cartier divisor, so blowing the chart up in it is an isomorphism; by tag 0GTY that
blowup is the restriction `b⁻¹(U) → U` of `b`. -/
@[stacks 0F8W "the affine-chart case: over an affine chart contained in the locally free locus
`W` the centre in which tag 0GTY blows the chart up is locally generated by a power of the
equation of the divisor, hence an effective Cartier divisor, so blowing the chart up in that
centre is an isomorphism"]
theorem isIso_blowUpToBase_of_le_locallyFreeLocus (C : AffineChart S)
    (hCW : C.U.1 ≤ S.locallyFreeLocus) :
    IsIso (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf) :=
  C.isIso_blowUpToBase_blowupCentreIdealSheaf
    (C.exists_away_map_blowupCentre_eq_span_pow_of_le_locallyFreeLocus hCW)

end AffineChart

/-- A morphism is an isomorphism over an open subscheme as soon as it is an isomorphism over
every member of a family of open subschemes covering it: being an isomorphism is Zariski local
on the target. -/
private theorem isIso_pullback_snd_of_cover {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) (W : Y.Opens)
    {ι : Type*} (U : ι → Y.Opens) (hcover : ∀ x ∈ W, ∃ i, x ∈ U i ∧ U i ≤ W)
    (hiso : ∀ i, U i ≤ W → IsIso (Limits.pullback.snd f (U i).ι)) :
    IsIso (Limits.pullback.snd f W.ι) := by
  classical
  let cover : W.toScheme.OpenCover := Scheme.Cover.mkOfCovers {i : ι // U i ≤ W}
    (fun i => (U i.1).toScheme) (fun i => Y.homOfLE i.2) (by
      intro x
      obtain ⟨i, hx, hUW⟩ := hcover x.1 x.2
      exact ⟨⟨i, hUW⟩, ⟨x.1, hx⟩, Subtype.ext (by simp)⟩)
  refine IsZariskiLocalAtTarget.of_openCover (P := MorphismProperty.isomorphisms Scheme)
    cover fun i => ?_
  show IsIso (Limits.pullback.snd (Limits.pullback.snd f W.ι) (Y.homOfLE i.2))
  have h : IsIso (Limits.pullback.snd f (Y.homOfLE i.2 ≫ W.ι)) := by
    rw [Scheme.homOfLE_ι]
    exact hiso i.1 i.2
  have hcomp : IsIso ((Limits.pullbackLeftPullbackSndIso f W.ι (Y.homOfLE i.2)).hom ≫
      Limits.pullback.snd f (Y.homOfLE i.2 ≫ W.ι)) := inferInstance
  simpa only [Limits.pullbackLeftPullbackSndIso_hom_snd] using hcomp

/-- A morphism which over an affine chart is the blowing up of the chart in a centre whose
blowup morphism is an isomorphism is itself an isomorphism over that chart. -/
private theorem isIso_pullback_snd_of_isoBlowUp {X' : Scheme.{u}} {b : X' ⟶ S.X}
    {C : AffineChart S}
    (e : Limits.pullback b C.U.1.ι ≅ AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf)
    (he : e.hom ≫ AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf
      = Limits.pullback.snd b C.U.1.ι)
    (h : IsIso (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf)) :
    IsIso (Limits.pullback.snd b C.U.1.ι) := by
  rw [← he]
  infer_instance

/-- **Stacks tag 0F8W.**  In Situation 0F8S let `W ⊂ X` be the maximal open subscheme over
which the cohomology sheaves of `M` are locally free.  A morphism `b : X' ⟶ X` which over
every affine chart `(U, A, f, M^•)` of the triple is the blowing up of `U` in the product
`∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` of its determinantal ideals — as the morphism of tag 0GTY is — is an
isomorphism over `W`, provided every point of `W` lies in an affine chart contained in `W`. -/
@[stacks 0F8W "the general form, over an arbitrary morphism which has the affine-chart \
description of tag 0GTY: a morphism which over every affine chart is the blowing up of that \
chart in the product of its determinantal ideals is an isomorphism over `W`, for an open `W` \
covered by the affine charts contained in it. The tag for the morphism tag 0GTY produces, with \
both descriptions discharged, is \
AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.isIso_pullback_snd_goodBlowupToBase_locallyFreeLocus"]
theorem isIso_pullback_snd_locallyFreeLocus {X' : Scheme.{u}} (b : X' ⟶ S.X)
    (hchart : ∀ C : AffineChart S, ∃ e : Limits.pullback b C.U.1.ι ≅
        AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf,
      e.hom ≫ AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf
        = Limits.pullback.snd b C.U.1.ι)
    (hcov : ∀ x ∈ S.locallyFreeLocus, ∃ C : AffineChart S,
      x ∈ C.U.1 ∧ C.U.1 ≤ S.locallyFreeLocus) :
    IsIso (Limits.pullback.snd b S.locallyFreeLocus.ι) := by
  refine isIso_pullback_snd_of_cover b S.locallyFreeLocus (fun C : AffineChart S => C.U.1)
    hcov fun C hCW => ?_
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hchart C
  exact isIso_pullback_snd_of_isoBlowUp S e he (C.isIso_blowUpToBase_of_le_locallyFreeLocus hCW)

namespace IsGoodBlowup

variable {S}
variable {X' : Scheme.{u}} {b : X' ⟶ S.X}

/-- **The universal-property half of Stacks tag 0F8W.**  Let `b : X' ⟶ X` have properties (1)
and (2) of tag 0GTY, and let `V ⊂ X` be an open subscheme whose inclusion is good for the
triple.  If moreover the restriction `b⁻¹V ⟶ X` of `b` is good for the triple, then `b`
restricts to an isomorphism `b⁻¹V ⟶ V`.

The inclusion of `V` lifts uniquely through `b`, and the lift lands in `b⁻¹V`; the lift and the
restriction of `b` are mutually inverse, one composite because `V.ι` is a monomorphism, the
other because `(b ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι ≫ b` has a unique factorization through `b`. -/
theorem isIso_resLE_of_isGoodOver (hb : S.IsGoodBlowup b) (V : S.X.Opens)
    (hV : S.IsGoodOver V.ι) (hVb : S.IsGoodOver ((b ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι ≫ b)) :
    IsIso (b.resLE V (b ⁻¹ᵁ V) le_rfl) := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk, -⟩ := hb.existsUnique_lift V.ι hV
  have hmem : ∀ v : V.toScheme, k.base v ∈ b ⁻¹ᵁ V := by
    intro v
    show b.base (k.base v) ∈ V
    have h : b.base (k.base v) = V.ι.base v := by rw [← hk]; rfl
    rw [h]
    exact v.2
  have hrange : Set.range k.base ⊆ Set.range (b ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι.base := by
    rintro _ ⟨v, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨⟨k.base v, hmem v⟩, rfl⟩
  refine ⟨IsOpenImmersion.lift (b ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι k hrange, ?_, ?_⟩
  · -- the restriction of `b` followed by the lift is the identity of `b⁻¹V`
    have h1 : (b.resLE V (b ⁻¹ᵁ V) le_rfl ≫ k) ≫ b = (b ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι ≫ b := by
      rw [Category.assoc, hk, Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι]
    obtain ⟨w, -, huniq⟩ := hb.existsUnique_lift ((b ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι ≫ b) hVb
    rw [← cancel_mono (b ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι, Category.assoc,
      IsOpenImmersion.lift_fac (b ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι k hrange, Category.id_comp]
    exact (huniq _ h1).trans (huniq _ rfl).symm
  · -- the lift followed by the restriction of `b` is the identity of `V`
    rw [← cancel_mono V.ι, Category.assoc, Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι,
      ← Category.assoc, IsOpenImmersion.lift_fac (b ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι k hrange, hk, Category.id_comp]

/-- **Stacks tag 0F8W reduced to its two unformalized inputs.**  A morphism `b` with properties
(1) and (2) of tag 0GTY is an isomorphism over the locally free locus `W`, once the inclusion of
`W` is known to be good for the triple and goodness is known to restrict to the open subscheme
`b⁻¹W` of `X'`. -/
theorem isIso_resLE_locallyFreeLocus (hb : S.IsGoodBlowup b)
    (hW : S.IsGoodOver S.locallyFreeLocus.ι)
    (hWb : S.IsGoodOver ((b ⁻¹ᵁ S.locallyFreeLocus).ι ≫ b)) :
    IsIso (b.resLE S.locallyFreeLocus (b ⁻¹ᵁ S.locallyFreeLocus) le_rfl) :=
  hb.isIso_resLE_of_isGoodOver _ hW hWb

end IsGoodBlowup

end AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation

